`awaiting-clarification` is a member of the `in-spec` superstate, so a run parked on unanswered
questions can be cancelled without the status declaring a `cancelled` edge of its own.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  tracker:
    driver: cli
-- fixtures/cwd/run/index.md --
---
title: "Demo"
status: awaiting-clarification
return_to: drafting
---

# Demo
-- cmd --
booping playbook-transition groom cancelled --workdir run
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
awaiting-clarification → cancelled
frontmatter: status=cancelled
script commit-plan: ok
script tracker-sync: ok
-- stderr --
-- expected/cwd/run/index.md --
---
title: "Demo"
status: cancelled
return_to: drafting
---

# Demo
